.org/hamrheadcorvette/{size}/32965_2.png", "created_at": "2024-06-26T16:32:27.012Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-packager\" data-username=\"jjames\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"123699\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/jjames/48/28140_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jerry James:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Many of these supported sagemath</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The Sagemath topic has come up in the past, is it now recommended to go with the container style builds? Makes more sense.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/sagemath/sage/?tab=readme-ov-file#sagemath-docker-images\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/2X/b/bad3e5f9ad67c1ddf145107ce7032ac1d7b22563.svg\" class=\"site-icon\" data-dominant-color=\"\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/sagemath/sage/?tab=readme-ov-file#sagemath-docker-images\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/344;\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/2/a/2a34a89c2a5ece332c1fb202a9b0ec92a590392e_2_690x345.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" data-dominant-color=\"ECEDF4\" width=\"690\" height=\"345\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://github.com/sagemath/sage/?tab=readme-ov-file#sagemath-docker-images\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub - sagemath/sage: Main repository of SageMath. Now open for Issues and...</a></h3>\n\n  <p>Main repository of SageMath. Now open for Issues and Pull Requests. - sagemath/sage</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>or the venv :</p>\n<aside cla